From d38c98e7b1c574397d8223bc85f5e5a1941a2c4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Baris Dinc <barisdinc@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 19:51:45 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] package: dvbs2-tx: New package

DVB-S2 QPSK modulator for the PlutoSDR: reads an MPEG transport stream,
encodes it (CCM, single TS input stream, normal or short FECFRAMEs, all
QPSK code rates, optional pilots, roll-off 0.35/0.25/0.20) and writes root
raised cosine shaped I/Q samples to the AD936x TX DMA through libiio, or
to a file.

The output is bit exact with the GNU Radio gr-dtv DVB-S2 transmitter for
all code rates and frame sizes, and the shaped I/Q decodes with leandvb.
The LDPC tables are taken from gr-dtv (GPL-3.0-or-later).

Null packets are inserted when the input is slower than the channel. BCH
encoding and pulse shaping are table driven: a 1 MS/s stream needs ~11 %
of one Cortex-A9 core.
